 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "matrix is a list of m equal-length strings (row r, column c is matrix[r][c]) and s is a non-empty string. For each start cell (r, c) and each direction among right (0, +1), down (+1, 0) and down-right diagonal (+1, +1), the pair counts when the |s| cells (r + i*dr, c + i*dc), i = 0..|s|-1, all lie in the matrix and spell s. Return the number of counted pairs (so a one-character s counts every matching cell three times).",
